5
# ir_diff: programs where the two x86 paths disagree, held so the count cannot grow. Since the slice-9
# flip (#980) the sides are the DEFAULT, which selects from the shared IR, and `x86-legacy`, the legacy
# emitter alone (`ir_diff: sides default=ir other=x86-legacy`). MEASURED on native x86_64 (GitHub gate
# run 43310061101, part ir) at #1604 restacked onto main aa45ef19, Stage1 built by the seed: corpus 2623
# programs, with-ir=756, ir-fns=1354, agree=751, disagree=5 (build=4 exit=1 stdout=0), verify-failed=0,
# dump-failed=1 (test/issue926_const_qualified_same_name_ok.al, the front-half crash every path has,
# #1567, recorded in scripts/known-deviations.tsv).
#
# It was 4 and it is 5 because the flip's #1579 fixture is new: every row below is the LEGACY path
# being wrong, and the default answers what the fixture states and what aarch64, riscv64 and wasm
# answer. A row leaves when the legacy emitter goes (docs/ir.md §7.2), or by being fixed there.
#
#   legacy refuses, the default runs (the four #1022 stopgaps, `## expect: run N` in each file):
#     test/deep_field_agg_enum_reject.al                legacy build 1   default run 42
#     test/deep_field_agg_var_reject.al                 legacy build 1   default run 42
#     test/packed_in_plain_struct.al                    legacy build 1   default run 20
#     test/reject_local_name_two_aggregate_types.al     legacy build 1   default run 109  (#406)
#   legacy answers a value no arm computes, the default traps (`## expect(x86_64): trap`):
#     test/issue1579_match_no_arm_traps.al              legacy run 255   default run 132  (#1579)
#
# ir_diff prints all five as UNEXPLAINED: its `oracle` (scripts/fixture_oracle.sh) reads only the
# legacy header shapes (`## build_reject`, `## Expected exit: N`) in the first 30 lines, never the
# `## expect:` directive these files state. Every row is explained above, by its file's own directive.
#
# Lowering the number means fixing a row, not editing this file.
